{"timestamp": 1778694184.2475288, "duration_sec": 2.524397850036621, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "What does it mean to be confused? What exactly is happening in our brains and in reality?"], [0, "I want you to give this question some thought while you're listening to this episode. And then I want you to imagine how this might apply to your interactions with other developers, perhaps your manager, or if you were a manager, your direct reports, the company you lead."], [0, "I want you to think about the role of perception in the work you do. My name is Jonathan Cutrell. You're listening to Developer T. And the goal of this show is to help driven developers find clarity, perspective, and purpose in their careers. So think about this question. What does it mean to be confused? A simple assertion to kind of guide you in this is to recognize that"], [0, "That confusion doesn't exist outside of someone's mind. And in this we are including the fact that animals can become confused. But confusion is a problem of perception."], [0, "And it's not even really a problem when you look at it from this frame because it's very easy to see that confusion can lead to learning. Confusion, for example, in a child might lead to curiosity. But in our professional lives, we tend to see confusion as a sign of weakness or perhaps a lack of preparation."], [0, "The truth is that we all have gaps in our knowledge, that we all have moments of confusion, even about things that perhaps at one point we actually knew a lot about."], [0, "It's possible that our perception has changed about even the same subjects that we have developed knowledge around in the past. And so it makes sense that we should be kind and perhaps even invite confusion to be a more regular part of our work. So how can we do this for ourselves and for others, perhaps most importantly?"], [0, "That's what we're going to talk about right after we talk about today's sponsor, Linode. Whether you're working on a personal project or managing your enterprise's infrastructure, Linode has the price, support, and scale that you need to take your project to the next level. With 11 data centers worldwide, latency is not going to be a serious issue. They have S3 compatible storage options and their next generation network."], [0, "Leno delivers the performance you expect at a price that you don't, and they're going to give you $20 worth of credit just for being a listener of Developer Tea. Now, their nano plans start as low as $5 a month, and of course, that goes all the way up to dedicated CPU plans or GPU compute plans"], [0, "block storage, go and check it out. Head over to linode.com slash developer T to get started today. Use the code developer T2020 to get that $20 worth of credit. That's developer T2020. Thanks again to Linode for sponsoring today's episode of Developer T."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Coding"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["confusion", "perception", "brain", "reality", "learning", "curiosity", "professional development", "software developers", "management", "workplace communication", "knowledge gaps", "career growth", "cloud hosting", "enterprise infrastructure", "data centers", "object storage", "sponsorship", "decision making"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
