ect. Because Veterans of the Long War, you get Oath plus Pact, which is obviously a very good combo when you're getting sustained hits or lethal hits. So yeah, it doesn't feel like you get as much in this list, do you? But obviously he's got, uh, some AC/DC\u2014 no, okay, just, uh, just rocking the Vindicators and some Noise Marines. Okay, interesting. It'll be interesting to see how Brian does. Brian's obviously a very good player as well, uh, and he's got the\u2014 ah, that's right, he's got the Weaponized Hatred, which is the, uh, double O at the moment there as well. And he's still playing Hieron, which\u2014 but he's not playing 60 points enhancement, I think. Honestly, for a one-time oath, it's interesting. I think that the Deathwatch one is, uh, 40 points, uh, as well. So fair enough. Interesting. Yeah, it's, uh, so we've got some really cool developments. This is called the Pyro Cup, uh, Maine 2026, guys, if you want to look up that tournament. Uh, a lot of, uh, very good players there. You know, John Lennon is playing. He's playing a very similar list to I played in New Zealand here. Uh, he's playing in, in Gladius as well. Uh, oh no, he's playing Blades of Ultramar. Okay, sorry, that's interesting. Uh, so Combi Lieutenant Marnius, but he's playing the kind of\u2014 oh, Ballistas Drednoughts."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Gaming"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["warhammer", "army lists", "unit points", "wounds", "infiltrators", "weapons", "hand flamer", "meltagun", "necrons", "tournament meta", "detachments", "chaos marines", "competitive gaming", "tabletop strategy", "army synergy", "list building", "international tournaments", "rule optimization"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778702856.851342, "duration_sec": 1.9135067462921143, "validator_hotkey": "5GQyFzvtVMw9X45t6dvUFgR9unFpDCccPPCiAoqJrtPuC8my", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "Like how many boyfriends has she had? What kind of like experience is going on here in life? And that's an interesting thing about this case because from what we understand, it seems that this girl didn't necessarily grow up in the best of environment. She's running away multiple times. That's a whole other conversation. What's inspiring her to constantly run away. But the fact that she kind of had"], [0, "from what we understand, a hard life, probably grew up a bit faster than everybody else, maybe did act a bit more mature than her age. But that seems to be such a thing with this case. And unfortunately, with young people who end up having to mature before their actual age says that they're old enough, they carry themselves differently. They carry themselves with a little more maturity. And it seems that the adults in the room around..."], [0, "don't recognize that, or they recognize it and they accept it when they really shouldn't. Nobody should be looking at a 13-year-old girl and going, oh, well, she's just more mature for her age, so we're just gonna treat her like an adult going forward. That's not okay, that's never okay, and I don't care who you are, especially the parents shouldn't be treating her that way, but it seems everybody in her orbit was treating her that way."], [0, "Yeah. And that's, you know, one of the things I'm not knocking all men, of course, but I remember being 12 and having predatory 30 year olds, you know, trying to give me rides home from school. And it's very seductive when you're a young teen girl and you're surrounded by predatory men. Yeah."], [0, "who will always say, oh, but you look older, you act older, you seem more mature. And as I've talked in my book, I met my first husband at 15, and he was 25. And, you know, and married him shortly thereafter. And one thing I heard from so many people, well, it's okay, because you're so mature."], [0, "And it wasn't OK. And it was pseudo maturity. You know, it was all a facade. And I think it's a problem in our culture where there's a certain subset of men who who go after young girls because they have so much power over them and kids can be easily manipulated."], [0, "Yeah, I keep getting fixated right now on that word maturity that everyone keeps using with her and Siobhan, from your amazing book, from your background experience, mine to a much lesser degree. I think what happens is, and I'm curious about if you agree,"], [0, "And use that word maturity when you're referencing someone who's so much younger, 13, but went through a lot of trauma and has a lot of reps in problem solving. I think people are mistaking someone's ability to problem solve because they face so much trauma. They face so many challenges in life and no one to rely on, no one to help them feel safe, no one to help work through it."], [0, "So they're very adept and have life skills at solving problems to be safe, which looks like someone else who wants to manipulate their own mind and rationalize it as, well, they're just mature. No, actually, they're problem solving the chaos in their lives. Is that accurate? I think that's a really good point. They gain some skills in survival. And so they may at times speak in a way that seems more sophisticated than a 13-year-old"], [0, "Some 13-year-olds are still playing with Barbie dolls, you know, and others are out walking in the street and getting rides home from predatory men and presenting themselves as older. But it's not insight. It's not real maturity. Right."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["child exploitation", "predatory men", "underage girls", "grooming", "trauma", "runaway youth", "adult child relationships", "power imbalance", "manipulation", "false maturity", "survival skills", "cultural norms", "parenting", "adolescence", "mental health", "social work", "victim blaming", "decision making"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
