. This is what I'm saying, Joe. What are you saying? I'm coming from this place. I'm like this, no disrespect or whatever to Cat, but Who asked."], [1, "You? Shannon Sharpe did when he did that podcast."], [0, "Shannon Sharpe might have asked one question."], [1, "But Shannon Sharpe likes that. Like that in his relationship, he likes a lot of that. His, his people, they find questions. He's got a sheet of paper."]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["Comedy"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["podcasts", "comedians", "standup comedy", "humor", "interviews", "storytelling", "gossip", "exposing secrets", "drama", "online platforms", "talent", "entertainment industry", "media business", "black culture", "celebrity culture", "conflict", "communication", "ethics"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
