{"timestamp": 1778711682.6675453, "duration_sec": 4.7665932178497314, "validator_hotkey": "5C8LULGoFybR7ybg4S8qQkaaowGXFFja4KmMoSqwhxuAsn33", "task_type": "named_entities_extraction", "task_raw": {"mode": "testnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "named_entities_extraction", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "document", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "SEATTLE CITY COUNCIL\n600 Fourth Ave. 2nd Floor\nSeattle, WA 98104\nJournal of the Proceedings of the Seattle City Council\nTuesday, April 28, 2026\n2:00 PM\nPublic Hearing\nCouncil Chamber, City Hall\n600 4th Avenue\nSeattle, WA 98104\nCity Council\nJoy Hollingsworth, Council President\nDionne Foster, Member\nDebora Juarez, Member\nRobert Kettle, Member\nEddie Lin, Member\nAlexis Mercedes Rinck, Member\nMaritza Rivera, Member\nRob Saka, Member\nDan Strauss, Member\nChair Info: 206-684-8803; Joy.Hollingsworth@seattle.gov\n\nCity Council Meeting Minutes April 28, 2026\nA. CALL TO ORDER\nThe City Council of The City of Seattle met in the Council Chamber in City\nHall in Seattle, Washington, on April 28, 2026, pursuant to the provisions of\nthe City Charter. The meeting was called to order at 2:02 p.m., with Council\nPresident Hollingsworth presiding.\nB. ROLL CALL\nPresent: 7 - Foster, Hollingsworth, Kettle, Lin, Rinck, Rivera, Saka\nExcused: 2 - Juarez, Strauss\nC. PRESENTATIONS\nCouncilmember Foster presented a procl"]], "participants": null}}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "ner_001", "crc": 1321322, "title": "Extract named entities from documents", "name": "extract_named_entities", "description": "Identifies and extracts named entities from provided documents.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "ner", "prompt_template": "Extract all named entities from the provided document. Include the following entity types: PERSON, ORGANIZATION, LOCATION, and any other relevant entities. Return as comma-delimited list of entities with their types (e.g., 'John Smith (PERSON), ACM Corp (ORGANIZATION)). Only return the entities without any additional commentary.", "output_variable": "extracted_entities", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["seattle city council", "city of seattle", "joy hollingsworth", "dionne foster", "debora juarez", "robert kettle", "eddie lin", "alexis mercedes rinck", "maritza rivera", "rob saka", "dan strauss", "seattle city hall", "council chamber", "seattle", "washington", "city charter"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
{"timestamp": 1778711889.845835, "duration_sec": 2.507878541946411, "validator_hotkey": "5HNe4Yx7idMcgrsoPogLVko2AA8Pap33aNyXQhpwBxsS4H4Q", "task_type": "conversation_tagging", "task_raw": {"mode": "mainnet", "api_version": 2.1, "guid": "HIDDEN", "bundle_guid": "HIDDEN", "type": "conversation_tagging", "scoring_mechanism": "ground_truth_tag_similarity_scoring", "input": {"guid": "HIDDEN", "input_type": "conversation", "data": {"window_idx": -1, "window": [[0, "You either make that happen or let that happen somehow, someway. And Sonny Stiles isn't slipping you 12, so you have to go make that one happen. That might cost you 20. I don't know where Caleb Downs is going yet. I don't think the collection of keen and wise observers exactly know that either. Item eight. There's rumors that Reuben Bain is off the board. I don't believe that."], [0, "Arm length is a problem. The Cowboys have talked, we've talked about that three months ago. It's a thing, it's an issue. And the position switch, that's an issue. And the team that drafts him better have a complete grasp"], [0, "Oh, we have, everybody already knows all about the car wreck. That's not what I'm talking about. I'm not talking about what everybody knows about the car wreck. I'm talking about what everybody can't yet know about the car wreck, which is his psyche going forward. You don't know that. And the team that drafts Reuben Bain better make sure they figure that out."], [0, "Item nine. There's a reason to take a linebacker at 20. False. Do the Cowboys have a hole there? Of course they have a roster hole there. If you don't get Stiles in the top 12, then you try again later and you move around for Rodriguez or Hill or Allen, but you don't have to do it at 20. And by the way, if you don't get it done at all,"], [0, "then you go back to my prediction of the Cowboys solving this somehow, some way. Now, I thought they would do it before the draft, but now can I stretch it out four days? Two weeks from now, the Cowboys will have a linebacker. Maybe it'll happen during the draft with who they select. Maybe it'll happen during the draft with a trade, or maybe it'll happen"], [0, "in the wake of the draft when they didn't get that done. And so they do the veteran one way or the other, but I don't have to be desperate enough to take, like we know all about Jacob Rodriguez, another guy that we've talked about for months, high floor, questionable ceiling. As I said to, uh,"], [0, "Jordan Schultz last night on Fish at Six. By the way, thank you so many of you for watching that and for spreading the word about real Cowboys talk here on this channel. And thanks to Jordan for hanging out with us as well. That was fantastic. More of that sort of thing, by the way, to come in the next week. Once he once Rodriguez ran his 40 at the combine and it was good."], [0, "Now it's not just about the floor. Now the ceiling looks a little better, but I'm not doing it at 20. And finally, and I see a few of you talking about Jerry. What Jerry's gonna do in this draft is, guys, I understand the trap. I understand why we fall in the trap, why you do. But if a media person is telling you about what Jerry's gonna do in this draft,"], [0, "don't buy what that person's selling. When a media person starts a sentence like that, his insight is false. The scouts under Will McClay will build the board with guidance from the coaching staff. Jerry Jones does not build the board. Jerry Jones' job is to listen and then to rubber stamp the decisions."], [0, "You're hearing a lot about, this is gonna be a Christian Parker draft. That's no different than it ever is. The coordinators have a big voice here. Coordinators have a big voice in helping Will McClay build the board. The buck stops with Jerry Jones, but it stops with a big rubber stamp. So make sure that your experts are telling you that it's Will McClay's draft"]], "participants": []}, "input_categories": ["News & Politics"]}, "prompt_chain": [{"step": 0, "id": "12346546888", "crc": 1321321, "title": "Infer tags from a conversation window", "name": "infer_tags_from_a_conversation_window", "description": "Returns tags representing the conversation as a whole from the window received.", "type": "inference", "input_path": "conversation", "prompt_template": "Analyze conversation in terms of topic interests of the participants. Analyze the conversation (provided in structured XML format) where <p0> has the questions and <p1> has the answers. Return comma-delimited tags. Only return the tags without any English commentary.", "output_variable": "final_output", "output_type": "List[str]"}], "example_output": {"tags": ["guitar", "barn", "farm", "nashville"], "type": "List[str]"}}, "result": {"tags": ["nfl draft", "dallas cowboys", "linebacker", "draft board", "scouting", "player evaluation", "roster needs", "trade scenarios", "first round pick", "nfl combine", "team coordinators", "front office", "sports media", "risk assessment", "injury recovery", "decision making", "talent development", "organizational leadership"], "vectors": null}, "error": null}
